notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-31T06:43:13.658Z","harness:claude-code","Decision reconfirmed against the shipped host rather than against the earlier spec note: pm append targets the body, so any command that used it for metrics would conflict on every concurrent write. The rule holds and now has a named counterexample attached to it."
files[1]{path,scope,note}:
  index.ts,project,Metrics append through repeatable note mutations only
tests[1]{command,scope}:
  "name=two real Git branches merge independently appended run metrics without loss,result=pass",project
close_reason: Decision is enforced by implementation and a real two-branch merge test.
